module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.TateResolution.SquareZeroDerivationFromLift
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.TateResolution.SquareZeroLiftDifferential
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.DividedPowers.TateResolution.TowerPresentation

/-! # The square-zero lift exists, and Tag 09PS

Let `q : R' → R` be a surjection of commutative rings whose kernel is the principal ideal
generated by `f : R'`, and let `(A, 𝒜, γ, d)` be a graded divided power polynomial algebra over
`R[xᵢ]` with a differential compatible with its divided powers. The preceding files of this
directory build, piece by piece, a lift of `(A, 𝒜, γ, d)` across `q`:

* the algebra `B` with its grading, its divided powers and the comparison morphism `π : B → A`
  (`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/SquareZeroLiftData.lean`),
* the operator `D` on `B` lifting `d`
  (`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/SquareZeroLiftDifferential.lean`),
* the kernel of `π` and the comparison map `κ`, given a divided power polynomial presentation of
  `B` (`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/LiftKernel.lean`),
* and that presentation
  (`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/DividedPowers/TateResolution/TowerPresentation.lean`).

This file collects them into the single predicate they were cut out of,
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.IsDividedPowerSquareZeroLift`, and feeds the result to
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.squareZeroExtensionDerivationOfLift`. That discharges the last
hypothesis of Tag 09PS: nothing is assumed about a lift any more, because one is produced.

## Main definitions

* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftComparisonMap` — the comparison map `κ : ker π → A/IA` of
  the lift, with its presentation hypothesis supplied by
  `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftPresentation`.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.squareZeroExtensionDerivation` — the derivation of degree minus
  two on `A/IA`, together with the whole construction Tag 09PS retains.

## Main results

* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftIsDividedPowerSquareZeroLift` — the lift built in this
  directory is a divided power square-zero lift. Each of the twelve clauses is a proved fact
  about one of its four components.
* `DividedPowers.TateResolution.exists_squareZeroLift` — the existence statement, in the form
  that quantifies over the carrier and its instances. This is what Tag 09PU consumes.

## Implementation notes

The two clauses `mem_ker_iff` and `kappa_apply` are the only ones needing freeness of `B`, and
they are the only ones whose source lemma takes extra arguments: a divided power polynomial
presentation of `B`, a degreewise bijection of its variables with those of `A`, and the
identification of its generators with the variables of the lift. All three are supplied by
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftPresentation`,
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftPresentationIndexEquiv` and
`DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftPresentation_generator`, so no hypothesis survives. They have
to be written out at the two fields rather than left to unification: the fields' statements do
not mention the presentation, so there is nothing for it to be inferred from.

Three of the tag's hypotheses are not consumed by any step: `(ker q) ^ 2 = ⊥` and the two
finiteness assumptions on the variable sets. The kernel of the comparison morphism is `f · B`
because it is the ideal generated by `ker q`, with no condition on that ideal, and the quotient
by `I · A` is forced by the cofactor of a kernel element being determined only modulo the
annihilator of `f` — again with no condition. The hypotheses are kept because the tag states
them; the statement proved is therefore the tag's, and the construction happens to be slightly
more general.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09PS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PS)
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace DividedPowers.TateResolution

universe u v w z

attribute [local instance] GradedDPAlgebra.ring GradedDPAlgebra.algebra
  GradedDPAlgebra.graded GradedDPAlgebra.strict

attribute [local instance] gradedLimitGradedAlgebra gradedLimitStrictlyGradedComm

section Lift

variable {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} {A : Type w} {σ : Type z}
  [CommRing R'] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
  (q : R' →+* R) {f : R'} {𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A} [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] [IsStrictlyGradedComm 𝒜]
  {γ : DividedPowerStructure 𝒜} {ι : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] A}
  (hpoly : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial 𝒜 γ ι)

/-- The comparison map `κ : ker π → A/IA` of the lift, where `I` is the image under `q` of the
annihilator of `f`. This is `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftKappa` with its presentation
hypothesis supplied by `DividedPowers.TateResolution.liftPresentation`. -/
public noncomputable def liftComparisonMap (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f}) :
    RingHom.ker (liftRingHom q hpoly) →+ A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A :=
  liftKappa q hpoly hf (liftPresentation hpoly) (liftPresentationIndexEquiv hpoly)
    (liftPresentation_generator hpoly)

/-- The comparison morphism carries each generator of the presentation of the lifted algebra to
the corresponding variable of `A`. This is the clause of Tag 09PS matching up the variables of
the two presentations. -/
public theorem liftRingHom_liftPresentation_generator (n : ℕ) (j : hpoly.indices n) :
    liftRingHom q hpoly
        ((liftPresentation hpoly).generator ⟨n, liftPresentationIndexEquiv hpoly n j⟩) =
      hpoly.generator ⟨n, j⟩ := by
  rw [liftPresentation_generator hpoly n j, liftRingHom_variable]

section Differential

variable (d : A →ₗ[R] A) [IsGradedDerivation 𝒜 d] [IsCompatibleWithDifferential γ d]

/-- **The lift built in this directory is a divided power square-zero lift of `(A, 𝒜, γ, d)`
across `q`.** Each of the twelve clauses is a proved fact about one of its four components: the
algebra and the comparison morphism of `SquareZeroLiftData.lean`, the operator `D` of
`SquareZeroLiftDifferential.lean`, the kernel computation and the comparison map of
`LiftKernel.lean`, and the presentation of `TowerPresentation.lean`. -/
public theorem liftIsDividedPowerSquareZeroLift (hq : Function.Surjective q)
    (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f}) :
    IsDividedPowerSquareZeroLift q f 𝒜 γ d
      (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).grade (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).gamma
      (liftRingHom q hpoly) (liftDerivation q hpoly d hq)
      (liftComparisonMap q hpoly hf) where
  surjective_base := hq
  surjective := liftHom_surjective q hpoly hq
  map_algebraMap := liftHom_algebraMap q hpoly
  map_mem_grade := liftHom_mem_grade q hpoly
  mem_ker_iff := liftRingHom_eq_zero_iff q hpoly hf (liftPresentation hpoly)
    (liftPresentationIndexEquiv hpoly) (liftPresentation_generator hpoly)
  D_eq_zero := liftDerivation_eq_zero q hpoly d hq
  D_mem_grade := liftDerivation_mem_grade q hpoly d hq
  D_leibniz := liftDerivation_leibniz q hpoly d hq
  map_D := liftRingHom_liftDerivation q hpoly d hq
  kappa_apply := liftKappa_apply q hpoly hf (liftPresentation hpoly)
    (liftPresentationIndexEquiv hpoly) (liftPresentation_generator hpoly)
  map_dpow n b hb := (liftHom_dpow q hpoly n b hb).symm
  D_dpow := liftDerivation_dpow q hpoly d hq

include hpoly in
/-- **A graded divided power polynomial algebra with a compatible differential has a divided
power square-zero lift across a surjection with principal kernel.** This is the component of
Tag 09PS that asserts the existence of the lift, and it is what Tag 09PU consumes.

The carrier is quantified together with its ring, algebra, grading and graded-commutativity
instances, which are fields of the bundled algebra the construction produces rather than
instances in their own right. They are supplied here as those fields rather than by instance
search: the carrier of the colimit is a reducible abbreviation ending in a `DirectLimit`, so a
search against it unfolds to the `DirectLimit` instances and exhausts the heartbeat budget. -/
public theorem exists_squareZeroLift (hq : Function.Surjective q)
    (hf : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f}) :
    ∃ (B : Type (max u v w z)) (hB : Ring B),
      letI : Ring B := hB
      ∃ hAlg : Algebra R' B,
        letI : Algebra R' B := hAlg
        ∃ (ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B) (hGr : GradedAlgebra ℬ),
          letI : GradedAlgebra ℬ := hGr
          ∃ hComm : IsStrictlyGradedComm ℬ,
            letI : IsStrictlyGradedComm ℬ := hComm
            ∃ (δ : DividedPowerStructure ℬ) (π : B →+* A) (D : B →ₗ[R'] B)
              (κ : RingHom.ker π →+ (A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A)),
              IsDividedPowerSquareZeroLift q f 𝒜 γ d ℬ δ π D κ :=
  ⟨(liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).carrier, (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).ring,
    (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).algebra, (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).grade,
    (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).graded, (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).strict,
    (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).gamma, liftRingHom q hpoly, liftDerivation q hpoly d hq,
    liftComparisonMap q hpoly hf, liftIsDividedPowerSquareZeroLift q hpoly d hq hf⟩

end Differential

end Lift

/-- **The degree-minus-two derivation of Tag 09PS.** Let `q : R' → R` be a surjection of
commutative rings whose kernel is generated by a single element `f` of square zero, let
`(A, 𝒜, γ, d)` be a graded divided power polynomial algebra over `R[xᵢ]` with a differential
compatible with its divided powers, and let `I` be the image under `q` of the annihilator of `f`.
Then `A/IA` carries an `R`-linear operator `θ` which obeys the Leibniz rule, lowers degrees by
two, and vanishes in degrees zero and one.

The construction the source retains is part of the statement: `θ` is the square of an operator
`D` lifting `d` to a divided power polynomial algebra `B` over `R'[xᵢ]` on the same variables,
compared into `A/IA` by division by `f`. -/
@[stacks 09PS]
public noncomputable def squareZeroExtensionDerivation
    {R' : Type u} {R : Type v} {A : Type w} {σ : Type z}
    [CommRing R'] [CommRing R] [Ring A] [Algebra R A]
    (q : R' →+* R) (hq : Function.Surjective q)
    (f : R') (hker : RingHom.ker q = Ideal.span {f})
    (_hsq : (RingHom.ker q) ^ 2 = ⊥)
    (𝒜 : ℕ → Submodule R A) [GradedAlgebra 𝒜] [IsStrictlyGradedComm 𝒜]
    (γ : DividedPowerStructure 𝒜)
    (d : A →ₗ[R] A) [IsDifferentialGradedAlgebra 𝒜 d] [IsCompatibleWithDifferential γ d]
    (ι : MvPolynomial σ R →ₐ[R] A)
    (hpoly : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial 𝒜 γ ι)
    (_hfinite₀ : Finite σ)
    (_hfinite : ∀ n : ℕ, Finite (hpoly.indices n)) :
    { θ : (A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A) →ₗ[R]
        (A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A) //
      (∀ x y : A, ∃ u v : A,
        θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = Submodule.Quotient.mk u ∧
        θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk y) = Submodule.Quotient.mk v ∧
        θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk (x * y)) =
          Submodule.Quotient.mk (u * y + x * v)) ∧
      (∀ (n : ℕ) (x : A), x ∈ 𝒜 (n + 2) →
        ∃ y : A, y ∈ 𝒜 n ∧
          θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = Submodule.Quotient.mk y) ∧
      (∀ (x : A), x ∈ 𝒜 0 → θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = 0) ∧
      (∀ (x : A), x ∈ 𝒜 1 → θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) = 0) ∧
      (∃ (B : Type (max u v w z)) (hB : Ring B),
        letI : Ring B := hB
        ∃ hAlg : Algebra R' B,
          letI : Algebra R' B := hAlg
          ∃ (ℬ : ℕ → Submodule R' B) (hGr : GradedAlgebra ℬ),
            letI : GradedAlgebra ℬ := hGr
            ∃ hComm : IsStrictlyGradedComm ℬ,
              letI : IsStrictlyGradedComm ℬ := hComm
              ∃ (δ : DividedPowerStructure ℬ)
                (ι' : MvPolynomial σ R' →ₐ[R'] B)
                (hpolyB : GradedDividedPowerPolynomial ℬ δ ι')
                (e : ∀ n : ℕ, hpoly.indices n ≃ hpolyB.indices n)
                (π : B →+* A) (D : B →ₗ[R'] B)
                (κ : RingHom.ker π →+ (A ⧸ squareZeroAnnihilatorSMul q f A)),
            Function.Surjective π ∧
            (∀ r' : R', π (algebraMap R' B r') = algebraMap R A (q r')) ∧
            (∀ p' : MvPolynomial σ R',
              π (ι' p') = ι (MvPolynomial.map q p')) ∧
            (∀ (n : ℕ) (j : hpoly.indices n),
              π (hpolyB.generator ⟨n, e n j⟩) = hpoly.generator ⟨n, j⟩) ∧
            (∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ ℬ n → π b ∈ 𝒜 n) ∧
            (∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ positiveEvenPart ℬ →
              π (δ.dpow n b) = γ.dpow n (π b)) ∧
            (∀ b : B, π b = 0 ↔ ∃ c : B, b = algebraMap R' B f * c) ∧
            (∀ (b : B), b ∈ ℬ 0 → D b = 0) ∧
            (∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), b ∈ ℬ (n + 1) → D b ∈ ℬ n) ∧
            (∀ (i j : ℕ) (b c : B), b ∈ ℬ i → c ∈ ℬ j →
              D (b * c) = D b * c + (-1 : R') ^ i • (b * D c)) ∧
            (∀ (n : ℕ) (b : B), n ≠ 0 → b ∈ positiveEvenPart ℬ →
              D (δ.dpow n b) = D b * δ.dpow (n - 1) b) ∧
            (∀ b : B, π (D b) = d (π b)) ∧
            (∀ (b : B) (hb : algebraMap R' B f * b ∈ RingHom.ker π),
              κ ⟨algebraMap R' B f * b, hb⟩ =
                Submodule.Quotient.mk (π b)) ∧
            (∀ b : B, ∃ hb : D (D b) ∈ RingHom.ker π,
              θ (Submodule.Quotient.mk (π b)) = κ ⟨D (D b), hb⟩)) } :=
  squareZeroExtensionDerivationOfLift q f 𝒜 γ d ι hpoly
    (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).grade (liftAlgebra (R' := R') hpoly).gamma
    (liftCoefficientAlgHom (R' := R') hpoly) (liftPresentation hpoly)
    (liftPresentationIndexEquiv hpoly) (liftRingHom q hpoly) (liftDerivation q hpoly d hq)
    (liftComparisonMap q hpoly hker)
    (liftIsDividedPowerSquareZeroLift q hpoly d hq hker)
    (liftRingHom_coefficient q hpoly) (liftRingHom_liftPresentation_generator q hpoly)

end DividedPowers.TateResolution

end
